<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43515" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭnārĭus</span></b> ,
		a, um. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			Adj.
			semen, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to seed</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seminarium pilum,</span>”
				<i>for bruising seed</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 10, 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sēmĭnārĭum</span></b> ,
				ii, n., <i>a
			nursery</i>, <i>nursery-garden</i>, <i>seed-plot</i>, <i>seminary.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 18,
				27, 71, § 295</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cato, R.
				R. 46</span></i>; <i><span class="en">48</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 29</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 5, 6, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 2, 16</span></i>; <i><span class="en">11, 2, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Arb.
				1, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 1</span></i>
			et saep.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">seminarium rei publicae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Off. 1, 17, 54</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fons et seminarium triumphorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Pis. 40, 97</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Catilinarium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Cat. 2, 10, 23</span></i>
			; so, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicum (veterani),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Phil. 13, 2, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senatūs (equites),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					42, 61, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">exiguum militum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 6,
					12</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hostilis exercitus (Hispania),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Flor.
					2, 6, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ducum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Curt.
					8, 6, 6</span></i>
			: dulce hilaritatis (vinum), Varr. ap.
				<i><span class="en">Non. 28, 22</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scelerum omnium (Bacchanalia),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
				39</span></i>
			 epit.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">omnium malorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. Mag. 74, p. 321, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rixarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hier. Ep. 27, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">repudii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. in Helv. 20</span></i>
			.</div>
